  "description": "As a tool for a racing cyclist,\n\nthis frame is world-class. We offer the Team Issue as a frame-and-fork in\n\nseven sizes. It’s the very frame the kick-butt-and-take-names Mercury\n\nteam rides. Same frame, not a replica. We like to sell what we race. The Mercury\n\nCycling Team dominates US racing on Fuji Team Issue bicycles. The fastest\n\nsprinter in North America, Mercury’s Gord Fraser, races a Team Issue.\n\nThis year, as Mercury travels to Europe, our bike could be equally successful\n\nover there.These frames are made from Easton Taperwall Scandium alloy tubes.\n\nSeat stays are carbon fiber, chain stays Easton aluminum. The Reynolds Ouzo\n\nPro fork has the special-order carbon fiber steerer.",
